# Code Style & Quality Standards

- Use Ruff for Python formatting (88 char line length, Python 3.11+ features)
- Use Prettier + ESLint for TypeScript (100 char, single quotes, trailing commas)
- Always make minimal, surgical changes - avoid large refactors
- NEVER delete commented code without explicit permission
- Always add comments to explain complex logic and business rules
- Write proper function documentation for all public APIs
- Fix code quality errors immediately - user prefers clean code without warnings
- Use `|` union syntax over `Union` in Python type hints
- Use Google-style documentation strings for Python functions and classes
